1
00:00:11,710 --> 00:00:13,240
I guess so.

2
00:00:15,120 --> 00:00:19,409
It‘s really hitting me
that I'm dating a girl.

3
00:00:19,410 --> 00:00:20,950
It feels nice.

4
00:00:27,540 --> 00:00:28,540
I don't know,

5
00:00:29,720 --> 00:00:30,720
I'm thinking,

6
00:00:32,140 --> 00:00:36,470
I'm really happy right now.

7
00:00:42,200 --> 00:00:45,470
Am I really happy?

8
00:01:37,500 --> 00:01:45,000
"How Do We Relationship?"

9
00:01:50,000 --> 00:01:55,500
(Episode 1: I'll Go Out With You)

10
00:01:59,080 --> 00:02:01,460
The basketball club is a blast!
Come check us out!

11
00:02:01,980 --> 00:02:04,900
We're the science club! We do lots
of fun stuff. Please come check us out!

12
00:02:06,080 --> 00:02:11,560
If you don't join a club,
you'll never make any friends.

13
00:02:14,860 --> 00:02:16,430
Sorry. Excuse me.

14
00:02:18,700 --> 00:02:20,000
Are you okay?

15
00:02:20,780 --> 00:02:22,000
I'm fine.

16
00:02:23,210 --> 00:02:24,560
They're really shoving these flyers at us.

17
00:02:24,580 --> 00:02:27,180
Seriously. They hand out so
many just for them to get tossed.

18
00:02:31,940 --> 00:02:33,880
Thank you.

19
00:02:36,820 --> 00:02:37,820
Wow.

20
00:02:37,940 --> 00:02:39,250
Nice cleavage.

21
00:02:48,140 --> 00:02:49,669
That's so bad.

22
00:02:49,670 --> 00:02:51,400
First day of school.

23
00:02:53,640 --> 00:02:55,999
It is what it is.

24
00:02:56,000 --> 00:02:57,210
It was right in front of my face.

25
00:02:58,280 --> 00:03:00,300
Hey, knock it off.

26
00:03:01,020 --> 00:03:03,286
- One more time! One more time!
- That short-haired girl is pretty cute, right?

27
00:03:03,310 --> 00:03:06,080
Totally my type.

28
00:03:08,040 --> 00:03:09,040
What's their deal?

29
00:03:10,240 --> 00:03:11,240
Hey.

30
00:03:11,360 --> 00:03:14,099
Miwa, be honest.
You're actually super popular, aren't you?

31
00:03:14,100 --> 00:03:15,760
How many boyfriends have you had so far?

32
00:03:16,630 --> 00:03:17,630
Huh?

33
00:03:18,620 --> 00:03:19,490
Where did that come from?

34
00:03:19,491 --> 00:03:21,360
I'm just curious.

35
00:03:24,060 --> 00:03:26,100
Well...

36
00:03:27,500 --> 00:03:28,500
Well?

37
00:03:29,660 --> 00:03:30,660
Ah...

38
00:03:30,980 --> 00:03:31,980
It's not that.

39
00:03:32,120 --> 00:03:33,120
Um...

40
00:03:33,220 --> 00:03:34,220
How should I put this?

41
00:03:34,580 --> 00:03:36,110
I don't know if it counts as dating.

42
00:03:36,760 --> 00:03:39,719
We were supposedly dating,
but it was kind of a situationship.

43
00:03:39,720 --> 00:03:40,919
Huh?

44
00:03:40,920 --> 00:03:41,920
Like, it's complicated?

45
00:03:41,921 --> 00:03:43,490
Like, I shouldn't pry?

46
00:03:43,500 --> 00:03:46,120
Yeah... let's go with that.

47
00:03:47,560 --> 00:03:49,890
Miwa, you're amazing.

48
00:03:50,360 --> 00:03:52,860
You look like you could
bag any guy you want.

49
00:03:54,030 --> 00:03:56,630
That's not true at all.

50
00:03:57,930 --> 00:03:58,930
I...

51
00:03:59,640 --> 00:04:02,500
I've never actually had
my feelings reciprocated.

52
00:04:03,410 --> 00:04:04,569
Huh?

53
00:04:04,570 --> 00:04:08,360
Alright, let's begin today's lecture.

54
00:04:28,000 --> 00:04:29,500
Inuzuka.

55
00:04:39,470 --> 00:04:42,040
Why not start a new romance then?

56
00:04:42,280 --> 00:04:43,220
Huh?

57
00:04:43,221 --> 00:04:44,450
You're being too loud.

58
00:04:44,810 --> 00:04:46,720
Ah... sorry.

59
00:04:47,620 --> 00:04:49,980
That's what you get for saying
weird things out of nowhere.

60
00:04:50,040 --> 00:04:51,290
No, I mean...

61
00:04:51,520 --> 00:04:54,560
I was wondering if we should go to
this welcome party.

62
00:04:55,260 --> 00:04:56,260
Hm?

63
00:04:56,830 --> 00:05:00,960
(Looking for a new romance? We're the Light Music
Club!) The Light Music Club. That's for bands, right?

64
00:05:01,380 --> 00:05:02,380
I actually...

65
00:05:02,500 --> 00:05:04,270
was in a band back in high school.

66
00:05:04,300 --> 00:05:06,640
So I figured I'd keep playing in college.

67
00:05:10,640 --> 00:05:13,440
I might want to join too.

68
00:05:14,270 --> 00:05:15,270
Really?

69
00:05:16,120 --> 00:05:17,120
Yeah.

70
00:05:17,210 --> 00:05:20,880
I've never played an instrument,
but I listen to a lot of rock music.

71
00:05:21,620 --> 00:05:22,620
You do, Miwa?

72
00:05:22,620 --> 00:05:23,200
Yeah.

73
00:05:23,201 --> 00:05:24,550
That's so unexpected.

74
00:05:26,720 --> 00:05:27,890
I get it.

75
00:05:28,460 --> 00:05:30,330
You were influenced by an ex, weren't you?

76
00:05:30,360 --> 00:05:32,480
The complicated boyfriend
you were just talking about.

77
00:05:34,000 --> 00:05:36,600
He wasn't my boyfriend.

78
00:05:37,430 --> 00:05:38,670
He wasn't?

79
00:05:39,430 --> 00:05:41,370
I see. Wait.

80
00:05:41,540 --> 00:05:42,910
Did I guess wrong?

81
00:05:43,170 --> 00:05:44,210
Huh? Then who was it?

82
00:05:44,220 --> 00:05:45,220
Your dad?

83
00:05:51,340 --> 00:05:52,340
Play a card! Play a card!

84
00:05:52,350 --> 00:05:55,220
- I did, I did!
- Come on, keep playing!

85
00:05:55,520 --> 00:05:57,850
Let me think! Let me think!

86
00:05:58,280 --> 00:06:00,520
Did you hear that?

87
00:06:00,820 --> 00:06:01,460
Hm?

88
00:06:01,461 --> 00:06:03,789
We're forming a band with these guys.

89
00:06:03,790 --> 00:06:04,830
Huh? We are?

90
00:06:04,860 --> 00:06:07,800
Listen up, everyone!
Starting from here, we have Mikkun,

91
00:06:08,260 --> 00:06:09,830
Tsuruta, and Lucha.

92
00:06:11,170 --> 00:06:15,740
Ah, um, I'm Inuzuka Miwa.

93
00:06:17,210 --> 00:06:18,310
Nice to meet you all.

94
00:06:20,640 --> 00:06:21,739
Do you have a boyfriend, Miwa?

95
00:06:21,740 --> 00:06:22,959
Huh? What's your type?

96
00:06:22,960 --> 00:06:25,290
Wait. What kind of guy
do I have to be to date you?

97
00:06:25,620 --> 00:06:28,320
- You have zero chance.
- My bad.

98
00:06:28,520 --> 00:06:31,180
- You're definitely out of the running.
- That's not true!

99
00:06:31,240 --> 00:06:32,659
- I have a shot, right?
- Come on, tell us!

100
00:06:32,660 --> 00:06:33,660
Um...

101
00:06:34,790 --> 00:06:37,090
I don't have a boyfriend.

102
00:06:38,260 --> 00:06:40,160
As for my type...

103
00:06:41,200 --> 00:06:42,200
Sorry.

104
00:06:42,700 --> 00:06:45,369
- I don't really know either.
- Hey, come on!

105
00:06:45,370 --> 00:06:46,679
Wait, Miwa, you really don't have one?

106
00:06:46,680 --> 00:06:47,680
What do you mean you don't know?

107
00:06:47,681 --> 00:06:49,000
That's so surprising.

108
00:06:49,910 --> 00:06:50,910
Huh?

109
00:06:51,170 --> 00:06:52,110
- What about me?
- But honestly,

110
00:06:52,140 --> 00:06:54,239
- Pick me, pick me!
- Let a guy dream, will ya?

111
00:06:54,240 --> 00:06:55,410
No way.

112
00:06:55,810 --> 00:06:57,679
You guys are way too thirsty.

113
00:06:57,680 --> 00:07:00,479
Miwa is shy,
so give her a break.

114
00:07:00,480 --> 00:07:01,480
Right?

115
00:07:01,750 --> 00:07:03,190
- No way, that's you.
- No, it's not!

116
00:07:03,680 --> 00:07:05,040
Band name? What about a band name?

117
00:07:05,720 --> 00:07:08,490
No, it's because of what you just said.

118
00:07:10,730 --> 00:07:13,400
The welcome party was really fun.

119
00:07:13,420 --> 00:07:14,800
And we successfully formed a band.

120
00:07:15,360 --> 00:07:18,879
Um, Saeko, thank you.

121
00:07:18,880 --> 00:07:19,880
Huh?

122
00:07:20,000 --> 00:07:23,270
Thanks for bailing me out
when I didn't know what to say.

123
00:07:23,680 --> 00:07:26,940
You're just too easy to read, Miwa.

124
00:07:27,440 --> 00:07:31,210
Everyone has things
they don't want to be grilled about.

125
00:07:32,140 --> 00:07:34,756
Do you have things like that too, Saeko?
Things you don't want to talk about?

126
00:07:34,780 --> 00:07:36,520
Of course I do.

127
00:07:36,540 --> 00:07:37,540
Ah.

128
00:07:37,620 --> 00:07:39,450
You're laughing at me, aren't you?

129
00:07:39,540 --> 00:07:40,860
No, I'm not.

130
00:07:43,860 --> 00:07:47,040
I guess it's fine
if I tell you, Miwa.

131
00:07:47,080 --> 00:07:48,080
I might as well tell you.

132
00:07:51,600 --> 00:07:55,900
To be honest,
I'm not really into guys.

133
00:07:56,270 --> 00:07:58,510
I prefer girls.

134
00:08:01,980 --> 00:08:02,980
Huh?

135
00:08:05,250 --> 00:08:06,300
Ah, sorry.

136
00:08:06,350 --> 00:08:07,180
No, it's not that.

137
00:08:07,220 --> 00:08:11,020
I mean, I have dated guys before.

138
00:08:18,160 --> 00:08:19,260
Me too.

139
00:08:20,460 --> 00:08:21,460
Huh?

140
00:08:23,980 --> 00:08:27,540
I like girls.

141
00:08:29,559 --> 00:08:32,262
S-Seriously? You're not just
saying that to agree with me, right?

142
00:08:32,286 --> 00:08:34,986
I wouldn't lie about something like this.

143
00:08:38,540 --> 00:08:40,020
Seriously?

144
00:08:48,260 --> 00:08:49,260
Wow.

145
00:08:49,490 --> 00:08:50,490
Well, in that case,

146
00:08:51,180 --> 00:08:54,000
There's no time like the present.
Why don't we try going out?

147
00:08:56,140 --> 00:08:59,600
Huh? Because it's a rare opportunity?

148
00:08:59,640 --> 00:09:03,199
I mean, meeting someone else who likes
girls is practically a miracle, right?

149
00:09:03,200 --> 00:09:06,480
Besides, I wouldn't have said anything
if it were anyone but you, Miwa.

150
00:09:08,320 --> 00:09:14,050
Do you mean, um...
you like me?

151
00:09:14,620 --> 00:09:15,620
Huh?

152
00:09:15,820 --> 00:09:16,820
Huh...

153
00:09:17,320 --> 00:09:19,190
I-I guess so.

154
00:09:19,780 --> 00:09:22,720
Like, as a friend, I guess.

155
00:09:23,580 --> 00:09:24,940
Probably?

156
00:09:25,820 --> 00:09:29,219
Wait, what about you, Miwa?
Do you like me?

157
00:09:29,220 --> 00:09:30,430
Or do you hate me?

158
00:09:31,600 --> 00:09:33,439
That's not fair, asking it like that.

159
00:09:33,440 --> 00:09:36,870
Since we both like each other as friends,
wouldn't it be nice to try dating?

160
00:09:38,710 --> 00:09:39,710
Huh...

161
00:09:42,310 --> 00:09:44,450
Never mind all that.
Which is it?

162
00:09:44,560 --> 00:09:46,580
Are we dating? Or not?

163
00:09:51,820 --> 00:09:57,060
Sure. If it's you, Saeko,
I wouldn't mind going out with you.

164
00:09:57,720 --> 00:10:00,560
Awesome!

165
00:10:02,660 --> 00:10:05,570
I'm so happy I get to date you, Miwa.

166
00:10:05,860 --> 00:10:07,370
I promise I'll treat you right.

167
00:10:10,040 --> 00:10:11,770
Awesome!

168
00:10:20,840 --> 00:10:23,650
- So annoying.
- You're up next, Miwa.

169
00:10:24,120 --> 00:10:25,420
Saeko.

170
00:10:28,720 --> 00:10:30,430
Huh? Where's Mikkun?

171
00:10:30,820 --> 00:10:33,420
He said he was still hungry
and went to the school store.

172
00:10:36,200 --> 00:10:38,770
Hey, about our band's lead singer...

173
00:10:38,900 --> 00:10:42,479
I definitely think Miwa should do it.
Even though Lucha really wants the spot.

174
00:10:42,480 --> 00:10:44,060
Why?

175
00:10:44,080 --> 00:10:46,180
You haven't even heard me sing.

176
00:10:46,240 --> 00:10:47,439
Draw four.

177
00:10:47,440 --> 00:10:51,150
Because draw four.

178
00:10:53,520 --> 00:10:55,720
Miwa has more stage presence.

179
00:10:57,380 --> 00:11:00,720
I'm actually not a very good singer.

180
00:11:01,500 --> 00:11:02,560
Draw four.

181
00:11:03,800 --> 00:11:07,530
- Tsuru!
- You're just being modest.

182
00:11:07,560 --> 00:11:09,479
I really can't sing at all.

183
00:11:09,480 --> 00:11:11,030
Really?

184
00:11:11,770 --> 00:11:13,070
I don't know,

185
00:11:13,580 --> 00:11:15,340
Are you two sitting a little too close?

186
00:11:16,880 --> 00:11:18,010
Are we?

187
00:11:18,680 --> 00:11:19,680
Well...

188
00:11:19,780 --> 00:11:21,180
Right?

189
00:11:21,540 --> 00:11:22,680
Well what?

190
00:11:23,410 --> 00:11:27,580
Because we're good friends.

191
00:11:27,620 --> 00:11:29,520
Right?

192
00:11:30,320 --> 00:11:32,300
I guess so.

193
00:11:34,820 --> 00:11:38,359
The First Annual Lead Singer Showdown!
One round takes all, no hard feelings!

194
00:11:38,360 --> 00:11:41,000
The Ultimate Vocal Battle Royale!

195
00:11:42,340 --> 00:11:43,284
That's way too long.

196
00:11:43,308 --> 00:11:47,419
Too wordy. Is there even going to be a second
one? Anyway, I nominate Miwa for lead singer.

197
00:11:47,773 --> 00:11:48,871
Saeko...

198
00:11:48,895 --> 00:11:52,999
Having Miwa as the lead singer
does sound like a good idea.

199
00:11:53,000 --> 00:11:57,109
I get that, but what about my image?

200
00:11:57,110 --> 00:12:02,480
But girls always tell me I'm a
great singer! So please let me do it!

201
00:12:08,480 --> 00:12:11,120
Being too good at
singing is actually a turn-off.

202
00:12:12,190 --> 00:12:13,460
He sings so well.

203
00:12:16,020 --> 00:12:17,020
That's me.

204
00:12:19,480 --> 00:12:20,480
That's my song.

205
00:12:21,880 --> 00:12:23,699
- It's me! It's my song!
- I'm better, right?

206
00:12:23,700 --> 00:12:25,099
Saeko.

207
00:12:25,100 --> 00:12:26,480
What's wrong with that?

208
00:12:28,380 --> 00:12:29,880
Miwa, what are you going to sing?

209
00:12:30,910 --> 00:12:32,450
Well...

210
00:12:33,560 --> 00:12:35,050
What should I pick?

211
00:12:38,440 --> 00:12:43,440
♪ Swaying back and
forth, just like a dream ♪

212
00:12:44,020 --> 00:12:49,020
♪ Swaying back and
forth, slowly melting away ♪

213
00:12:55,000 --> 00:12:57,039
See? I told you.

214
00:12:57,040 --> 00:12:59,419
I'm not very good at this.

215
00:12:59,420 --> 00:13:04,000
No, no, no. Well, you see...

216
00:13:04,020 --> 00:13:05,599
I thought it was great.

217
00:13:05,600 --> 00:13:09,119
Hey, can't you guys give a normal reaction?

218
00:13:09,120 --> 00:13:11,250
No, it's just that Miwa...

219
00:13:11,420 --> 00:13:15,620
Miwa, don't worry about it.
Being tone-deaf is no big deal.

220
00:13:17,390 --> 00:13:18,530
Whatever. It's fine.

221
00:13:20,260 --> 00:13:21,900
Let's just sing together.

222
00:13:22,500 --> 00:13:24,260
♪ Doing it ♪

223
00:13:24,400 --> 00:13:28,020
♪ Because our pace is different, BPM ♪

224
00:13:28,120 --> 00:13:32,320
♪ Matching the 83 beat,
taking a night walk with you ♪

225
00:13:32,380 --> 00:13:35,540
♪ Don't say anymore ♪

226
00:13:35,600 --> 00:13:38,399
♪ Do you know about the
"chronostasis illusion"? ♪

227
00:13:38,400 --> 00:13:40,779
You say you don't know.

228
00:13:40,780 --> 00:13:42,650
She's so good...

229
00:13:45,240 --> 00:13:48,120
Wow, that's so cool.

230
00:13:50,030 --> 00:13:51,030
That's insane.

231
00:13:51,980 --> 00:13:53,730
So cool.

232
00:13:55,200 --> 00:13:58,129
So Lucha is the lead
singer, and Miwa is on bass.

233
00:13:58,130 --> 00:14:00,400
Can I really do this?

234
00:14:00,460 --> 00:14:02,670
I don't think I have any musical talent.

235
00:14:03,570 --> 00:14:05,070
You'll be fine.

236
00:14:05,100 --> 00:14:07,880
For bass, as long as you have a
sense of rhythm, you can play it.

237
00:14:08,710 --> 00:14:10,610
Your rhythm just now was pretty good.

238
00:14:11,200 --> 00:14:13,050
Only my rhythm, though.

239
00:14:15,220 --> 00:14:16,920
Doesn't this suit Miwa perfectly?

240
00:14:18,500 --> 00:14:20,220
So cute.

241
00:14:20,500 --> 00:14:21,620
Looks good.

242
00:14:21,960 --> 00:14:23,830
Let me test it out for you.

243
00:14:24,660 --> 00:14:25,660
Huh? Can you?

244
00:14:26,900 --> 00:14:27,900
Excuse me.

245
00:14:28,440 --> 00:14:31,579
Can I try playing that white one?

246
00:14:31,580 --> 00:14:32,680
Yes, of course.

247
00:14:44,740 --> 00:14:45,850
Don't fall for me.

248
00:14:49,620 --> 00:14:51,750
Say something, will you?

249
00:14:51,850 --> 00:14:53,120
See?

250
00:15:00,300 --> 00:15:02,160
- Miwa.
- Yeah?

251
00:15:02,920 --> 00:15:04,430
Let's hold hands.

252
00:15:05,080 --> 00:15:06,080
Huh?

253
00:15:06,960 --> 00:15:08,340
Out here on the street?

254
00:15:08,370 --> 00:15:10,240
No one's looking.

255
00:15:10,440 --> 00:15:12,010
Plus, they're all strangers anyway.

256
00:15:15,160 --> 00:15:16,350
I guess it's fine.

257
00:15:27,220 --> 00:15:28,690
Saeko.

258
00:15:29,380 --> 00:15:31,990
Are you the really open type?

259
00:15:32,200 --> 00:15:36,460
Maybe I am.

260
00:15:37,800 --> 00:15:40,040
I mean, I've always been like this.

261
00:15:41,400 --> 00:15:44,310
But now I've decided to just
live my life without holding back.

262
00:15:47,420 --> 00:15:52,810
I used to struggle with having to
conform to society's expectations.

263
00:15:53,450 --> 00:15:56,220
But eventually, I realized
how stupid that was.

264
00:15:58,400 --> 00:15:59,500
Because I don't want...

265
00:15:59,620 --> 00:16:01,660
...a life full of holding back.

266
00:16:06,660 --> 00:16:07,700
What's wrong?

267
00:16:08,890 --> 00:16:09,890
Ah.

268
00:16:10,160 --> 00:16:11,170
Nothing.

269
00:16:12,480 --> 00:16:17,840
It's just the first time you've said
something so serious, Saeko. It surprised me.

270
00:16:18,840 --> 00:16:20,710
Oh, come on. What are you talking about?

271
00:16:22,080 --> 00:16:25,480
But I think I get it.

272
00:16:26,420 --> 00:16:29,620
Maybe we think the same way.

273
00:16:31,190 --> 00:16:34,440
We both want to live without
betraying our true feelings, right?

274
00:16:37,460 --> 00:16:38,460
Yeah.

275
00:17:09,200 --> 00:17:10,520
Saeko.

276
00:17:10,560 --> 00:17:11,560
Um...

277
00:17:12,360 --> 00:17:13,360
Yeah?

278
00:17:14,660 --> 00:17:15,660
Well...

279
00:17:16,570 --> 00:17:19,370
When you confessed to me before...

280
00:17:20,240 --> 00:17:22,700
...didn't you say you didn't
really see me that way?

281
00:17:23,340 --> 00:17:26,840
What about now?

282
00:17:27,820 --> 00:17:29,659
Huh? What?

283
00:17:29,660 --> 00:17:31,180
What's wrong? Why the sudden question?

284
00:17:33,160 --> 00:17:37,740
I want to know if your "like" feelings
have changed from friend to girlfriend.

285
00:17:40,120 --> 00:17:42,060
Why do you ask?

286
00:17:44,600 --> 00:17:49,030
I've always wanted a girlfriend.

287
00:17:49,060 --> 00:17:53,320
So when you said we should
date, I was really happy.

288
00:17:55,980 --> 00:17:58,910
But, how should I put it...

289
00:18:00,240 --> 00:18:06,580
It feels like we're only dating
out of compromise or convenience.

290
00:18:08,460 --> 00:18:11,890
Miwa, what exactly are you trying to say?

291
00:18:12,140 --> 00:18:13,140
Ah.

292
00:18:13,660 --> 00:18:14,660
Well...

293
00:18:15,990 --> 00:18:23,670
Basically, I don't know if this is how
love and dating are supposed to be.

294
00:18:24,000 --> 00:18:25,300
So I'm a bit confused.

295
00:18:25,800 --> 00:18:28,000
You're so serious, Miwa.

296
00:18:29,670 --> 00:18:32,570
My heart races when you touch me.

297
00:18:33,140 --> 00:18:37,180
But whether that's out of
romantic feelings or not...

298
00:18:40,650 --> 00:18:42,050
...I'm not sure.

299
00:18:44,550 --> 00:18:45,550
Listen.

300
00:18:46,270 --> 00:18:49,290
If you're thinking this
seriously about us...

301
00:18:49,360 --> 00:18:51,860
...doesn't that mean you already like me?

302
00:18:52,590 --> 00:18:53,669
Huh?

303
00:18:53,670 --> 00:18:55,860
I mean, you definitely like me, right?

304
00:18:58,670 --> 00:18:59,670
Eh.

305
00:19:00,410 --> 00:19:03,170
Does dating have to be so rigid?

306
00:19:03,690 --> 00:19:06,140
If it doesn't work out, we
can just break up, right?

307
00:19:07,810 --> 00:19:09,549
Why are you so casual about this?

308
00:19:09,550 --> 00:19:11,150
What's wrong with being a little casual?

309
00:19:11,450 --> 00:19:14,409
Can't we just try dating first?

310
00:19:14,410 --> 00:19:15,510
When it comes to love...

311
00:19:17,730 --> 00:19:21,490
Are you forcing yourself, Saeko?

312
00:19:23,110 --> 00:19:24,330
Not at all.

313
00:19:24,950 --> 00:19:27,870
But if you want to break
up, Miwa, I'll go along with it.

314
00:19:28,570 --> 00:19:33,770
But right now, I have absolutely
no intention of breaking up.

315
00:19:37,470 --> 00:19:40,540
I don't want to break up either.

316
00:19:41,970 --> 00:19:45,780
But when it comes to the confession...

317
00:19:46,010 --> 00:19:48,380
...I want a do-over.

318
00:19:48,720 --> 00:19:50,409
Why?

319
00:19:50,410 --> 00:19:53,890
I feel like I was acting too
high and mighty back then.

320
00:19:54,770 --> 00:19:56,360
I've been regretting it.

321
00:19:59,890 --> 00:20:01,130
What?

322
00:20:04,570 --> 00:20:05,570
Saeko.

323
00:20:08,900 --> 00:20:09,900
Yeah?

324
00:20:15,110 --> 00:20:16,350
Let's go out.

325
00:20:21,650 --> 00:20:22,650
Okay.

326
00:20:22,730 --> 00:20:24,220
I wouldn't mind dating you.

327
00:20:32,690 --> 00:20:34,169
Were you just nervous?

328
00:20:34,170 --> 00:20:35,850
Huh? No way.

329
00:20:48,610 --> 00:20:50,570
No way, I definitely can't play this.

330
00:20:51,110 --> 00:20:53,120
As a beginner, I actually...

331
00:20:54,070 --> 00:20:56,524
Miwa, want to practice together? We're
both in the rhythm section, after all.

332
00:20:56,548 --> 00:20:58,929
Practice with me. I've
played bass before, at least.

333
00:20:58,930 --> 00:20:59,930
Me too! Me too! Me too!

334
00:21:00,030 --> 00:21:01,070
You guys can pass.

335
00:21:01,130 --> 00:21:03,430
Lucha, you've never even played before.

336
00:21:03,530 --> 00:21:07,000
Alright, shut up. You're bothering Miwa.

337
00:21:07,710 --> 00:21:09,129
This has nothing to do with you, Saeko.

338
00:21:09,130 --> 00:21:10,900
Of course it does. I'm...

339
00:21:12,700 --> 00:21:13,700
Huh?

340
00:21:16,810 --> 00:21:17,810
I'm...

341
00:21:18,170 --> 00:21:20,480
...Miwa's bass master.

342
00:21:21,140 --> 00:21:22,210
Master?

343
00:21:22,810 --> 00:21:23,880
Is that so?

344
00:21:24,980 --> 00:21:26,150
I guess so.

345
00:21:27,570 --> 00:21:29,610
By the way, shouldn't you
guys be heading to class?

346
00:21:30,890 --> 00:21:33,310
Hurry up and get out.

347
00:21:34,070 --> 00:21:35,870
- Hurry up.
- Get ready, quick.

348
00:21:36,350 --> 00:21:38,450
- Move it.
- Stop dawdling.

349
00:21:39,260 --> 00:21:40,400
Saeko.

350
00:21:41,990 --> 00:21:43,190
Aren't you going to tell them?

351
00:21:44,570 --> 00:21:46,110
Well...

352
00:21:47,070 --> 00:21:50,140
If you tell the wrong people,
things can get pretty ugly...

353
00:21:52,910 --> 00:21:55,630
Lucha, you're still dragging your feet.

354
00:21:56,190 --> 00:21:59,050
- Hurry up.
- We're going to be late again.

355
00:22:00,750 --> 00:22:04,190
Saeko, how do I position my fingers here?

356
00:22:05,550 --> 00:22:07,820
- You hold it down here...
- Yeah.

357
00:22:25,130 --> 00:22:26,130
Miwa.

358
00:22:50,030 --> 00:22:51,400
Wait a minute.

359
00:22:52,570 --> 00:22:54,069
We're in the club room.

360
00:22:54,070 --> 00:22:55,830
Who cares? No one's looking.

361
00:22:56,850 --> 00:22:58,650
That's not the point.

362
00:22:59,670 --> 00:23:00,670
There should be more...

363
00:23:00,990 --> 00:23:01,990
...mood or something.

364
00:23:03,010 --> 00:23:04,010
Miwa.

365
00:23:04,790 --> 00:23:06,610
Don't tell me this is your first time?

366
00:23:10,550 --> 00:23:11,850
I don't know.

367
00:23:15,690 --> 00:23:16,730
Shut up.

368
00:23:38,350 --> 00:23:41,750
Ah, sorry. I accidentally saw that.

369
00:23:45,690 --> 00:23:47,159
(Next Episode)
One-month anniversary.

370
00:23:47,160 --> 00:23:48,590
Congratulations.

371
00:23:48,630 --> 00:23:50,969
I want to join this club.

372
00:23:50,970 --> 00:23:53,849
I really feel like we've been
missing each other lately.

373
00:23:53,850 --> 00:23:55,250
You think it's a hassle, don't you?

374
00:23:55,500 --> 00:23:56,500
Dealing with me.

375
00:23:57,910 --> 00:23:59,430
I want all of you, Miwa.
